WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.689 --> 00:00:05.620
Half the time we see any of The Walking Dead’s
survivors onscreen, they're covered in post-apocalyptic

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:07.069
filth and zombie sludge.

00:00:07.069 --> 00:00:11.169
So when their real-life counterparts clean
themselves up and hit the interview circuit,

00:00:11.169 --> 00:00:12.690
they're especially stunning.

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:16.539
They're even more unrecognizable in these
adorable throwback pictures from their youth.

00:00:16.539 --> 00:00:19.910
Here’s what The Walking Dead cast looked
like as kids.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.110
Andrew Lincoln

00:00:21.110 --> 00:00:25.050
Andrew James Clutterbuck hails from London,
and showed an interest in acting in his early

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:26.050
teens.

00:00:26.050 --> 00:00:29.400
He chose his stage name, Andrew Lincoln, after
studying at the Royal Academy of Dramatic

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:34.329
Art and landing his first real gig in an episode
of a U.K. sitcom called, Drop the Dead Donkey.

00:00:34.329 --> 00:00:39.289
It would be almost a decade before he landed
his second-most widely seen role to date as

00:00:39.289 --> 00:00:42.659
the lovesick, sign-holding, Mark in Love,
Actually.

00:00:42.659 --> 00:00:46.469
Since becoming Sheriff Rick Grimes for The
Walking Dead, Lincoln has shunned all other

00:00:46.469 --> 00:00:47.739
roles.

00:00:47.739 --> 00:00:49.289
Chandler Riggs

00:00:49.289 --> 00:00:53.730
Just seven when he first started packing heat
to battle the walkers, Chandler Riggs is a

00:00:53.730 --> 00:00:55.780
natural within the realm of the undead.

00:00:55.780 --> 00:01:00.260
It's also a been-there-done-that situation
for him, since his first role was in the short

00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:02.390
amateur film, Jesus H. Zombie.

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:06.200
The Walking Dead set was a homecoming for
him, as he's a native of Atlanta, Georgia,

00:01:06.200 --> 00:01:07.690
where the show is filmed.

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:13.191
Riggs is keeping the horror theme going, starring
in Mercy in 2014, as well as the 2016 home

00:01:13.191 --> 00:01:15.270
invasion flick, Keep Watching.

00:01:15.270 --> 00:01:16.780
Norman Reedus

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:21.570
After moving to L.A. and working as a motorcycle
mechanic, Norman Reedus was discovered at

00:01:21.570 --> 00:01:22.570
a party.

00:01:22.570 --> 00:01:27.370
It wasn’t long before he landed a role in
Guillermo del Toro's Mimic, ...and the 1997

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:29.540
film Floating, …. launching his career.

00:01:29.540 --> 00:01:33.840
Before The Walking Dead, he was best-known
for his role as Murphy Macmanus in The Boondock

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:34.840
Saints.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:38.330
Reedus' original audition was for the role
of Merle Dixon, but it'd already gone to actor

00:01:38.330 --> 00:01:39.400
Michael Rooker.

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:43.580
Show execs liked him so much that they created
Daryl Dixon for him, not knowing the character

00:01:43.580 --> 00:01:45.720
would become such a fan favorite.

00:01:45.720 --> 00:01:46.900
Melissa McBride

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:51.910
In the early '90s, Melissa McBride landed
her first role on an episode of Matlock, but

00:01:51.910 --> 00:01:54.550
she also worked behind the scenes as a casting
director.

00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:59.760
You may also recognize her from her appearance
as Dawson’s slightly-older-lady in Dawson’s

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:00.760
Creek.

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:04.230
McBride was chosen to star as Carol due to
her relationship with original showrunner

00:02:04.230 --> 00:02:08.530
Frank Darabont, who cast her in his adaptation
of Stephen King's The Mist.

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:09.540
Also in The Mist?

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:14.530
Laurie Holden, who played The Walking Dead’s
Andrea, and Jeffrey DeMunn, who played Dale.

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:15.530
Steven Yeun

00:02:15.530 --> 00:02:19.500
Though he was born in Seoul, South Korea,
Steven Yeun and his family moved to Saskatchewan

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:20.500
when he was a child.

00:02:20.500 --> 00:02:23.080
"Uh, this is the core of who I am, I have
brought a picture.

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:24.850
That's me."

00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:29.680
Yeun studied psychology in college, and his
parents hoped he'd pursue a career in medicine

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:30.680
or law.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:33.560
"Then your parents were not happy that you
chose this profession?"

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:40.700
"Uh, no, my parents are, are Korean and traditionally
uh, that first generation of Korean Americans

00:02:40.700 --> 00:02:44.910
aren't to happy with uh, the little curve
ball that you throw them."

00:02:44.910 --> 00:02:48.480
He had an interest in acting, though, and
moved to Chicago to pursue his interest in

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.640
improv, landing a gig with Second City before
relocating to Los Angeles.

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:56.590
Prior to Dead, he'd had a number of roles
in shows like The Big Bang Theory and Law

00:02:56.590 --> 00:03:01.110
&amp; Order: LA, but his biggest break happened
when he landed the part of Glenn Rhee… which

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:04.240
was only his second audition in LA.

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:05.480
Lauren Cohan

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:09.500
Although she was born in the U.S., Lauren
Cohan's family relocated to the U.K. when

00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:13.450
she was a teenager, so that’s why she still
speaks with a distinct accent when she's out

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:14.450
of character.

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:18.630
After studying drama in college, she launched
her career in the mid-2000s with films like

00:03:18.630 --> 00:03:20.980
Van Wilder 2 and Float.

00:03:20.980 --> 00:03:26.090
She gained more screen time as Bela in Supernatural
and a brief, albeit memorable stint on The

00:03:26.090 --> 00:03:30.340
Vampire Diaries before joining The Walking
Dead as Maggie Greene.

00:03:30.340 --> 00:03:31.800
Danai Gurira

00:03:31.800 --> 00:03:36.480
Born in Iowa and raised in her family's native
nation of Zimbabwe, Danai Gurira participated

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:38.800
heavily in her school's drama programs.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:43.489
She later studied psychology at Minnesota’s
Macalester College and achieved her M.F.A.

00:03:43.489 --> 00:03:46.030
at NYU's prestigious Tisch School of the Arts.

00:03:46.030 --> 00:03:50.930
Gurira became involved with the Broadway theater
scene as well—and is still active in theater.

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:55.610
Her harrowing play about the Liberian sex
slave industry, titled Eclipsed, was recognized

00:03:55.610 --> 00:03:57.890
by the 2016 Tony Awards.

00:03:57.890 --> 00:04:03.180
No stranger to action, Gurira also won the
role of Okoye, a royal guard in Marvel's Black

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:04.260
Panther.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:05.430
Jeffrey Dean Morgan

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:10.340
Seattle native Jeffrey Dean Morgan has made
a name for himself in both TV and film, perhaps

00:04:10.340 --> 00:04:14.480
best recognized as ill-fated heartthrob Denny
Duquette in Grey's Anatomy, and through his

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:18.130
recurring roles in Supernatural, Magic City
and The Good Wife.

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:22.910
The Walking Dead marks a maniacal new turn
for Morgan's screen presence, as he'd previously

00:04:22.910 --> 00:04:26.760
been known to play a relatively nice guy in
most of his prior projects.

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.000
Michael Cudlitz

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:32.900
Before he started rocking The Walking Dead’s
show's most meme-friendly facial hair as Abraham

00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:37.780
Ford, Michael Cudlitz had a few memorable
TV and movie moments on Beverly Hills 90210,

00:04:37.780 --> 00:04:40.020
Band of Brothers, and Southland.

00:04:40.020 --> 00:04:43.650
The latter earned him a Critic's Choice Award
in 2013.

00:04:43.650 --> 00:04:46.730
Since taking on the role of the troubled-but-beloved
Abe…

00:04:46.730 --> 00:04:53.900
"When you were uh, pouring the bisquick, you
trying to make pancakes?"

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:58.900
...Cudlitz has continued working on the small
screen, nabbing recurring guest roles in Ballers

00:04:58.900 --> 00:05:01.419
and House of Lies during his Dead downtime.

00:05:01.419 --> 00:05:02.419
Josh McDermitt

00:05:02.419 --> 00:05:06.640
On The Walking Dead, Eugene Porter might just
be unintentionally funny, but in real life,

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:10.010
Josh McDermitt's entire career can be attributed
to his humor.

00:05:10.010 --> 00:05:14.660
He got his start by calling into a local Phoenix
radio show before making a very brief appearance

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:17.410
on the comic competition show Last Comic Standing.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:22.230
He then moved into acting on the failed pilot
for Rehab for Rejects and the quickly-cancelled

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:27.680
sitcom Retired at 35 before making a two-episode
appearance on AMC’s Mad Men.

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:32.320
Finally, McDermitt landed the role of a lifetime
as The Walking Dead’s resident mullet.

00:05:32.320 --> 00:05:34.680
"The smartest man I ever met happened to love
my hair.

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:38.190
He said my hair made me look like and I quote,
a fun guy."

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:39.190
Thanks for watching!

00:05:39.190 --> 00:05:43.030
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:05:43.030 --> 00:05:46.300
And leave us a comment to let us know which
Walking Dead actor is your favorite...

